<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="003" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-03: Register missing OperationAccessPolicy keys + call-site completeness test</title>
    <phase>0 Enforcement Remediation</phase>
    <gate>after-001</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <status-note>RE-OPENED 2026-09-30 (owner Q7 approval, session 27), for its A-20 finance claim ONLY. The four policy keys and the completeness gate shipped here are correct and stay. But A-20's user-visible outcome, "finance endpoints resolve instead of always denying", is still false for GET /api/finance/matters/{matterId}/summary, which returns 403 for every caller. FinanceAuthorizationFilter passes the MATTER id into the document-only access data source, so the answer is always None. That is defect C8 (summary half). The completing work is task 130. See the amendments block.</status-note>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs on an authorization path (Spaarke.Core/Auth) and adds tests — FULL per root CLAUDE.md §8 (auth tag + TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>The missing keys and every call-site are exhaustively enumerated in finding A-20; implementation is mechanical against a closed list.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/** — a known contended path (task 004 modifies AuthorizationService.cs in the same directory).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001, 130</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Close findings A-3/A-20 policy-key half (spec FR-03, High): every operation string passed to an authorization filter must exist in OperationAccessPolicy, and an automated completeness test must keep it that way. Today "read", "finance.read", "finance.confirm", and "entity.associate_document" are absent, so OperationAccessRule unconditionally denies those endpoints ("unknown_operation").</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in the Spaarke.Core authorization seams (OperationAccessPolicy / OperationAccessRule) and xUnit. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>All four missing operation keys resolve in OperationAccessPolicy with least-privilege rights, and a completeness test enumerates every authorization-filter call-site operation string and asserts each resolves — so a future unregistered key fails the build, not production.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Finding A-20 (10-finding-confirmations.md) enumerated every operation string reaching AuthorizationService/OperationAccessRule against OperationAccessPolicy._operationRequirements (OperationAccessPolicy.cs:25-149). OperationAccessRule.EvaluateAsync:35-46 denies any unknown operation. Complete always-deny list: "finance.read" → FinanceEndpoints.cs:18,:51,:65; "finance.confirm" → FinanceEndpoints.cs:23,:37; "entity.associate_document" → EntityAccessFilter.cs:64 attached at OfficeEndpoints.cs:173; "read" → DataverseDocumentsEndpoints.cs:443, FileAccessEndpoints.cs:118 (eml-render), ChatDocumentEndpoints.cs:915 (archive ingest). All ResourceAccessRequirement operations wired in AuthorizationModule.cs:182-247 ARE present. FR-03 acceptance: automated test enumerates all filter call-sites and asserts each key resolves. NOTE: the unknown-operation DENY behavior itself is correct fail-closed design (NFR-01) and must not be weakened — the fix is registering the keys.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/Rules/OperationAccessRule.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/EntityAccessFilter.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/OperationPolicyCharacterizationTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="completed">Characterization tests pinning the unknown-operation denials, to be flipped here.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail-closed unknown-operation denial in OperationAccessRule MUST remain intact — this task registers keys; it does not soften the deny path. Scope: OperationAccessRule and OperationAccessPolicy.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Assign least-privilege rights per key: read-only endpoints get Read; mutating endpoints (finance.confirm, entity.associate_document) get Write-bearing requirements. Scope: the four new policy entries.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">The completeness test is MAINTAIN-class at a KEEP path; it must fail when a NEW call-site introduces an unregistered operation string (a real forcing function, not a snapshot of today's list only). Scope: the new test.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Spaarke.Core is consumed by the BFF (CLAUDE.md §10): report publish size vs baseline ~44.96 MB in PR; ceiling 60 MB (NFR-06). Scope: this task's PR.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>operation access policy</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-003-authorization-seams.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/10-finding-confirmations.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="unit-test-structure" location=".claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md">Test naming + structure</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load knowledge files; declare FULL rigor.</step>
    <step order="1">Re-verify the A-20 call-site list by grepping for authorization-filter operation strings across src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api (filters, ResourceAccessRequirement, EntityAccessFilter usages).</step>
    <step order="2">Add the four keys to OperationAccessPolicy with least-privilege AccessRights: "read" and "finance.read" → Read; "finance.confirm" and "entity.associate_document" → Write-bearing (match the semantics of comparable existing entries).</step>
    <step order="3">Author OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests: enumerate every operation string used at filter call-sites (scan mechanism of your choice: source scan of the Api tree, or a canonical registry the call-sites share) and assert each resolves via OperationAccessPolicy; include an explicit closed-list assertion covering the A-20 strings.</step>
    <step order="4">Flip the task-001 characterization tests: the four operations now resolve; unknown strings still deny.</step>
    <step order="5">Run full test suite; build green.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document rights-level decisions per key in projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the correct AccessRights for a key is ambiguous (e.g. finance.confirm could be Write or a finance-specific right), STOP and escalate the level choice per CLAUDE.md §6 rather than guessing high.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the grep sweep finds operation strings beyond the A-20 list that also fail to resolve, report them and add them to the fix — but escalate first if any belongs to another in-flight project's surface.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests — the existing BFF test project; no completeness/forcing-function test over OperationAccessPolicy exists (A-20 was found by manual enumeration).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — a new test file inside the existing project; this is test surface for existing code, not new production surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the completeness test, a future call-site introducing an unregistered operation string re-opens A-3/A-20 (unconditional 403) undetected — exactly the drift this test is the forcing function against (FR-03).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools><tool name="dotnet">Build + test</tool></tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/OperationPolicyCharacterizationTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">"read", "finance.read", "finance.confirm", and "entity.associate_document" each resolve in OperationAccessPolicy (FR-03 acceptance).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The completeness test enumerates every authorization-filter call-site operation string and asserts each resolves; it FAILS if a call-site uses an unregistered string.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an operation string NOT in the policy is still denied by OperationAccessRule (fail-closed preserved) — asserted by test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller whose rights do not meet a key's requirement is denied on that operation (e.g. Read-only caller on finance.confirm) — asserted by test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit tests pass; build green; publish size reported in PR and ≤60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>**COMPLETED 2026-08-21.** 4 keys registered; 15-test source-scanning completeness gate; 8 task-001
  characterizations flipped. Suite: BFF 10,617 / ArchTests 36 / Core 45, all green. Publish 43.65 MB
  compressed incl. PDBs (baseline 44.96 -- DOWN 1.31 MB; no package changes). 0 HIGH/CRITICAL CVE.

  RIGHTS DECISIONS (full rationale: notes/task-003-operation-rights-decisions.md):
  read -&gt; Read | finance.read -&gt; Read | finance.confirm -&gt; Write (NOT Create -- the sprk_invoice is a
  different entity than the authorized document) | entity.associate_document -&gt; **AppendTo** (the filter
  authorizes the TARGET entity and the operation attaches a document TO it; NOT Write -- saving an email
  to a matter does not modify the matter's own fields).

  ⚠️ AppendTo is the FIRST use of that flag in the policy, so it creates a binding obligation on TASK 005:
  map Dataverse AppendToAccess, or POST /api/office/save is permanently 403 while LOOKING fixed
  (insufficient_rights reads as legitimate). Recorded as a &lt;constraint source="task-003"&gt; on 005.

  SWEEP: re-derived the call-site list rather than trusting A-20 -- 22 Add*Filter extensions exist but only
  7 reach AuthorizeAsync; the 3 AI filters use IAiAuthorizationService (checks AccessRights.Read directly)
  and DataverseAuthorizationFilter uses IDataversePrivilegeChecker, so all are correctly out of scope.
  A-20's list CONFIRMED COMPLETE for active call-sites. Filed NEW finding **A-23** (escalation trigger 2):
  AddOfficeDocumentAccessFilter is a second orphaned filter (zero call-sites, doc examples "share"/"attach"
  unregistered) -- Low severity, delete alongside A-15 in task 018 (&lt;constraint source="task-003"&gt; added).

  DEVIATION: tests authored at tests/integration/auth/** (the ADR-038 KEEP path backfilled by task 001),
  not the POML's declared tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/AccessControl/ -- same CLAUDE.md 6.5 path C
  reasoning as task 001.

  Spec FR-03; findings A-3 + A-20 (policy-key half — the Read-ceiling half is task 005). The endpoints remain functionally broken for Write+ callers until 004/005 land; this task only guarantees key resolution and least-privilege requirements.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>

  <amendments date="2026-09-30" source="session 26 defect verification (C8, summary half) and owner Q7 approval in session 27 (notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md; notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md)">
    <verdict>RE-OPENED for the A-20 finance-summary claim. A-20 was attributed only to the missing
    "finance.read" key. Registering the key (correct, and it stays) moved the failure one layer down
    instead of removing it. notes/task-003-operation-rights-decisions.md records the filter as fixed; it
    is not. The completing work is task 130. No further code is authored under this id.</verdict>
    <amendment n="1" defect="C8" completing-task="130">
    The failure chain, verified against current code:
    (1) GET /api/finance/matters/{matterId}/summary is filtered with "finance.read"
    (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs:64-65; group filter at :18).
    (2) FinanceAuthorizationFilter takes matterId as ResourceId (src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs:66-67
    ExtractResourceId, :80 ResourceId, :122-123 matterId first).
    (3) AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs:28)
    asks the document-only data source. Its RPA target and fallback probe are sprk_documents
    (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseAccessDataSource.cs:373 DocumentEntitySetName, :793
    fallback probe). A matter id is not a document, so the result is None.
    (4) "finance.read" requires Read (src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs:167), so
    every honest caller gets 403.
    This fails closed, so it is an availability defect, not a disclosure. The entity-generic seam that
    answers the right question already exists: AuthorizationService.GetCallerRecordAccessAsync
    (AuthorizationService.cs:255, added by task 070). Task 130 moves the filter onto it with the correct
    entity set per route.</amendment>
    <amendment n="2">Out of this task's scope, but tracked by the same completing task so it is not lost:
    the recalculate IDOR (POST /api/finance/{matters|projects}/{id}/recalculate, auth-only groups at
    src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/FinanceRollupEndpoints.cs:28-31 and :47-50) is C8's other half.
    It was never part of A-20 and does not bear on this re-open. It belongs to task 130.</amendment>
    <acceptance-criteria-amended>
      <criterion testable="true">Task 130 is completed: a caller with Read on matter M gets 200 from GET /api/finance/matters/{M}/summary, and a caller without Read on M gets 403. Both asserted by test, with the authorization check evaluated against the MATTER, not a document.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Regression: the other routes in the same group (POST /invoice-review/confirm and /reject, GET /invoices/search, FinanceEndpoints.cs:22, :36, :50) still authorize against the entity their id actually names (document or invoice), and a caller without Read on that record still gets 403. Asserted by test; the summary fix must not re-point them at the matter.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Negative: the fail-closed unknown-operation denial and the completeness gate shipped by this task are unchanged, and their tests still pass.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev): an existing non-admin test user with Read on a matter loads that matter's finance summary, and gets 403 on a matter they cannot read. Recorded in notes.</criterion>
      <criterion testable="true">Only then are this task's status and its TASK-INDEX marker set back to completed, and scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1 is clean for id 003.</criterion>
    </acceptance-criteria-amended>
  </amendments>
  <amendments date="2026-10-05" source="owner round 59, 2026-10-05, BINDING (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md, 'Owner round 59'; evidence: notes/batch5-scope-review-2026-10-05.md, row 003)">
    <verdict>MERGED into 130's live gate. No separate work remains in this task. &lt;status&gt; stays pending until the absorbing gate passes; the task is then marked completed together with it, citing that gate's evidence.</verdict>
    <amendment n="1" title="Evidence">Already met by 130 (7c5c4e8a0, in integ and in the dev BFF 5e1fdcc0b): the finance summary route checks the matter (FinanceEndpoints.cs:81-82). No defect remains.</amendment>
    <amendment n="2" title="Closing gate">Live session A item 1: a non-admin with Read on a matter gets 200 on the finance summary; without Read, 403. When 130's live gate passes, mark this task completed with it.</amendment>
  </amendments>
</task>
